    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Root Cause\nThe bug was in how Commander.js parses global options. When you ran `frai gate init --ci`, Commander was consuming the global `--ci` option defined on the main `frai` command before the `gate` subcommand could receive it. This meant the `gate` subcommand's handler only received `['init']` instead of `['init', '--ci']`.\n\n## The Fix\nRemoved the redundant global `--ci` option from the main program (line 605 of `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`). Since both the `generate` and `scan` subcommands already define their own `--ci` options, the global option was unnecessary and was blocking the `gate` subcommand from receiving the flag.\n\n## Verification\n- Rebuilt the frai-cli package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested `frai gate init --ci` in a clean directory\n- Both files are now created as expected:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2705\n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2705\n\nThe workflow file contains the proper GitHub Actions configuration to run the gate on every PR.",
